- pubspec stamped to exactly the tag version;
- curated `## Unreleased` body folded under `## <version>`, no `## Unreleased` header surviving, older curated sections preserved newest-first;
- over-cap staged file trims oldest-first and keeps the fresh section (fixture with a ~300 KiB old section → staged file < 262144);
- missing `version:` line in the staged pubspec fails loud **with the invariant message** (this also surfaced a real gap: `set -e` killed the script on grep's exit 1 before the message — `stamp_staged_release.sh` now uses `|| true` so the loud `refusing to publish` error fires);
- the duplicate-section case you flagged: a repo CHANGELOG already carrying a curated `## <version>` section for the same version no longer renders twice — the stamper now drops a kept section whose header equals the fresh version (covered by its own test).

All 24 tests in the file pass.
"}

